From: rockbandPi
Subject: [PATCH] Make BASS callbacks IL2CPP compatible

IL2CPP can only pass delegates to native code when they point to static
methods marked [MonoPInvokeCallback]. YARG hands BASS lambdas and instance
methods, which Mono accepts but IL2CPP rejects at runtime with
"IL2CPP does not support marshaling delegates that point to instance
methods to native code". Song audio then fails to load and gameplay stays on
a black screen.

Turn every BASS callback into a static [MonoPInvokeCallback] method that
finds its object through BASS's user pointer, a GCHandle that is freed once
BASS can no longer call back:
- BassStreamProcedures: file close/length/read/seek for song streams
- BassStemMixer: normalization gain DSP and song end sync
- BassSampleChannel: sound effect end sync
- BassMicDevice: recording callback, and the attribute on the monitor gain DSP
---
diff --git a/Assets/Script/Audio/Bass/BassAudioManager.cs b/Assets/Script/Audio/Bass/BassAudioManager.cs
index 4e733860..5d6fdce6 100644
--- a/Assets/Script/Audio/Bass/BassAudioManager.cs
+++ b/Assets/Script/Audio/Bass/BassAudioManager.cs
@@ -630,9 +630,11 @@ namespace YARG.Audio.BASS
             // https://www.un4seen.com/forum/?topic=20148.msg140872#msg140872
             const BassFlags streamFlags = BassFlags.Prescan | BassFlags.Decode | BassFlags.AsyncFile | (BassFlags) 64;
 
-            streamHandle = Bass.CreateStream(StreamSystem.NoBuffer, streamFlags, new BassStreamProcedures(stream));
+            var procedures = new BassStreamProcedures(stream);
+            streamHandle = Bass.CreateStream(StreamSystem.NoBuffer, streamFlags, procedures, procedures.User);
             if (streamHandle == 0)
             {
+                procedures.Release();
                 YargLogger.LogFormatError("Failed to create source stream: {0}!", Bass.LastError);
                 return false;
             }
